      "id": "grammar-por-que-vs-porque",
      "kind": "grammar",
      "promptEs": "por qué / porque",
      "answerEn": "Por qué means “why”; porque means “because.”",
      "noteEn": "Write the question form as two words, with an accent on qué. Write the usual answer word porque as one word without an accent.",
      "tags": [
        "A1",
        "grammar",
        "questions",
        "spelling"
      ],
      "questionEn": "How do you write “why” and “because” in Spanish?",
      "example": {
